    'text' => 'Our Philosophy: Assume Eligibility We assume every applicant is eligible until we find disqualifying information This prevents eligible people from being turned away due to technicalities Eligibility checks are a process, not a gatekeeping moment 2. What Makes Someone Eligible? Category Requirements Geography Property must be in service area (Buncombe, Madison, Henderson, Haywood counties) Home Ownership Applicant must own the home (or have legal authority to authorize repairs) Primary Residence Must be primary residence, not rental or vacation property Income No lower limit. Upper limit varies by organization (typically 80% AMI) Cause of Damage Damage must be related to Hurricane Helene (September 2024) Household Size Counts residents 50%+ of the time Demographics No discrimination; special programs for veterans, elderly, disabled 3. The Eligibility Review Process Automated Check: System runs initial eligibility on submission Manual Review: Caseworker verifies documentation Organization Match: System finds best-fit organization (income, location, repair type) Final Determination: Assigned organization confirms eligibility 4. What Makes Someone Ineligible (Disqualifiers) Property outside service area Not a homeowner Not primary residence Previous assistance received for same repair Income exceeds all partner maximums Mobile home without lot ownership Under 18 without guardian consent 5. What If I\'m Denied? You will receive a clear explanation You can appeal with additional documentation You may be referred to other resources',
