    'excerpt' => 'Outline 1. What We Ask For (And Why) Information Why We Need It Contact Info To reach you about your application Home Address To verify location and serve your property Household S',
    'text' => 'Outline 1. What We Ask For (And Why) Information Why We Need It Contact Info To reach you about your application Home Address To verify location and serve your property Household Size To determine income eligibility Income To qualify for programs (no lower limit, upper limit varies) Home Ownership To confirm you can authorize repairs Demographics For grant reporting and program eligibility Repair Needs To assess scope of work Photos/Evidence To document damage and scope 2. What We DON\'T Ask For Social Security Number Bank account details Immigration status Criminal history Medical records 3. Privacy Protections Protection Description Encryption All PII encrypted at rest and in transit Role-Based Access Only assigned staff can see your information Audit Trail Every access is logged No Sharing Information never shared outside ARCHR organizations No Selling We never sell data to advertisers or brokers Warrant Required We don\'t share with law enforcement without a warrant 4. What is PPI (Protected &amp; Privileged Information)? All information you provide is considered private Protected under Privacy Act considerations Only used for your application and repair Never used for any other purpose 5. Your Rights View your data at any time Request corrections Request deletion (after case closure) Withdraw consent at any time Know who has accessed your data 6. The Consent Form You\'ll sign a consent form during intake This allows us to process your application You can revoke consent at any time If you revoke, we stop processing (but may still need to retain records) 7. What Happens When Your Case is Closed Data retained for 7 years (grant requirements) Then archived to cold storage At 10 years, permanently deleted You can request early deletion (some data may need to stay for compliance)',
  ),
  41 => 
